  "compiler_notes": [
    "Originally compiled as type=aggregate. Promoted to python_frame_function because the cell aggregation needs to JOIN reviewed scores with importance weights on evidence_id before grouping — a single aggregate node can't express that. The aggregation itself (weighted_mean, weighted_sum, count) is standard once the join is in hand.",
    "Methodology line 354 names a 'weighted cell score' but does not give the closed form. Reconstructed as weighted mean over (importance × recency).",
    "5-year hard cutoff (line 358) is enforced upstream by setting recency_weight=0 in importance_tagging for items older than 5 years."
  ]
